## CLAIM CHECKLIST — the REBUILT list; grade what the delta can reach, carry the rest

Grade every line the delta can reach, by its name. Carry a line forward only when you can
say why the delta cannot reach it, and say so per line. Lines 1-17 are the first audit's
checklist; G1-2 is restated for the new assert count, and G1-6 and G2-3 carry a note.
Lines 18-19 are new with the audit fixes.

1. **G1-1 — filed in words only.** The ruling filed a process-contract clarification as
   separate work. The change-set contains NO edit to any file outside the declared scope —
   in particular, no process contract changed.
2. **G1-2 — RED before green.** The record claims the RED baseline was captured against the
   report file restored from commit `0c1bbf7`, and the committed logs show exit 1 with PASS
   only on A4, A8, A14, then exit 0. Restated at this head: the selftest file defines
   exactly the FIFTEEN asserts A1–A15. `selftest-red.txt` and `selftest-green.txt` name
   A1–A14 at their capture heads; `selftest-a15-red.txt` and `selftest-a15-green.txt` name
   A15 red then green across the fix. Cite the logs; do not re-run them.
3. **G1-3 — the background file cannot count.** The fixture writes `tasks/bg.output` with
   three transcript-shaped assistant-usage lines INSIDE the fixture projects root; the
   report's usage scan reads only `.jsonl` transcripts, so a `.output` file can appear in no
   row; A3's expected totals are computed from what the fixture wrote, never hard-coded.
4. **G1-4 — ambiguity degrades.** An agent file whose OWN records name two or more distinct
   items keeps its branchless responses unattributed: the tree walk returns nothing for it,
   and it never inherits from its parent. A9 asserts both halves (branchless lines
   unattributed; branch-resolved lines keep their own items).
5. **G1-5 — no depth cap.** The parent walk (`Get-TreeItem`) terminates on a
   `parentAgentId` cycle by a visited set, and there is NO depth cap.
6. **G1-6 — inheritance is per spawn call.** A spawned agent inherits the item its session
   had resolved AT that spawn's tool-use id — not file-wide, not latest-wins. The fixture
   changes the session's held item between the U1 and U2 spawns, and A7 asserts the two
   inherit DIFFERENT items. The first audit graded this box FAIL; the AUD-1 fix addresses
   it — re-grade against the delta.
7. **G1-7 — vendor tables in JSON.** `-Json` emits the vendor aggregate tables (`codexRows`
   and `kimiRows`); the kimi join key is the BARE agent id, with the `agent-` file-name
   prefix stripped.
8. **G1-8 — the unattributed row is exact.** A11 computes the expected unattributed row
   from the fixture (X1's lines plus M1's branchless lines) and recomputes the printed
   percentage from the JSON totals, to the report's own rounding.
9. **G1-9 — the switches are protected.** A12 asserts `-Item` returns that item's rows
   only. A13 asserts `-Days 7` excludes exactly the fixture transcript whose
   `LastWriteTime` is set 40 days back (E1), which the default run includes. Meta files are
   ALWAYS all read, regardless of `-Days`.
10. **G1-10 — escaped decoys never resolve.** Branch discovery matches UNESCAPED
    `"gitBranch"` only; an escaped `\"gitBranch\"` inside a quoted tool result is never a
    branch fact. The fixture plants an escaped decoy naming `AI4DEV-999` inside O1's tool
    result, and A14 asserts no table names it. Check the regex character by character.
11. **D-1 — the scan is recursive.** The usage scan reads `agent-*.jsonl` recursively under
    each session's `subagents` tree, nested `workflows/wf_*` directories included;
    `tasks/*.output` and `*.meta.json` files are excluded; no file is counted twice. The
    fixture contains `workflows/wf_1/agent-W1.jsonl` with its meta beside it, and W1 joins
    A1's tree expectation and A3's totals.
12. **G2-1 — the stamp fallback is session-only.** The `$curStamp` fallback applies ONLY
    when the file is a session file (`-not $isAgent` at the fallback site). The fixture's
    M1 carries a stamp line naming the second fixture item BEFORE its branchless lines, so
    a leak turns A1, A9 and A11 red from the fixture's own bytes.
13. **G2-2 — the vendor join degrades on ambiguity.** The `$agentItem` assignment is
    SKIPPED for an agent file whose own records name two or more items. The fixture plants
    a `wd_agent-M1_*` kimi directory with distinctive amounts, and A10 asserts the kimi
    table holds exactly ONE row (the O1 join) whose output tokens equal the O1 wire sum
    alone.
14. **G2-3 — the spawn-context key carries the session (proven by measurement).**
    `$spawnCtx` is keyed by session PLUS tool-use id. A session file's id is its base name;
    an agent's session derives from its directory path (captured when the meta is read).
    First sighting wins WITHIN a session, never across sessions. The measurement behind
    this is committed at `loop/items/AI4DEV-80/artifacts/g2-3-probe.txt` — cite it, do not
    re-measure. The first audit graded this box FAIL on the first-sighting half; the AUD-1
    fix addresses it — re-grade against the delta.
15. **G2-5 — A1 asserts tokens, not only counts.** A1 asserts `OutputTok` on each of its
    rows, computed from the fixture's own measurements, never hard-coded.
16. **G2-6 — disproven, so nothing changed.** The percentage print site carries NO added
    culture-forcing, and the selftest's decimal assertion was NOT loosened. The probe
    behind this is committed at `loop/items/AI4DEV-80/artifacts/g2-6-probe.txt` — cite it.
17. **Stated code facts.** (a) The Temp `.output` scan and the file-name pairing pass are
    DELETED — no `.output` file is ever usage-scanned. (b) Role comes from meta
    `agentType`; a metaless agent reads `unmarked agent` and is announced in the output.
    (c) Per-response resolution order: own-record branch → (two items on one branch:
    unresolved) → tree → stamp (session files only) → unattributed. (d) The root-override
    parameters default to the previous hard-coded paths, and a `-Json` switch emits the
    aggregates.
18. **AUD-1 — the first sighting pins, resolved or not.** At the `$spawnCtx` sighting site,
    EVERY first sighting of a session-qualified `toolu_` id stores a value: the single
    resolved item when the session state (branch first, stamp fallback) resolves exactly
    one, the EMPTY STRING otherwise. A later occurrence of the same key never overwrites —
    the `ContainsKey` guard stands above the assignment. `Get-TreeItem` reads an empty
    stored value as unattributed and is unchanged by the fix. A15 covers this: the fixture
    plants a session whose spawn `toolu_` id first appears BEFORE any branch or stamp fact,
    which then resolves an item on its own record, and repeats the id in its tool result;
    the spawned branchless agent stays unattributed. The A15 session lives in an ISOLATED
